content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-104 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22871, filtered-water line",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end vibration is 7.6 mm/s. The applicable HF-300 criterion is Figure 3, vibration velocity in mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings. The reading is above the 7.1 mm/s RMS Zone C/Zone D boundary and within Zone D (7.1–11.0): 'Damage likely — stop the pump.' The Zone C restricted-operation/plan-maintenance response therefore does not apply. The manual requires both housings to be measured and the highest reading classified.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing-housing temperature is 84°C. For housing-surface temperature, the applicable limits are normal up to 70°C, alarm at 80°C and trip at 90°C. Thus 84°C exceeds the alarm limit but is below the trip limit; it is not within the normal range. The pump must nevertheless be stopped because of its Zone D vibration.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft-area leakage is approximately one drop per second. No numerical allowable leakage-rate limit is supplied. The applicable troubleshooting entry treats leakage at the shaft seal as a fault symptom and directs mechanical-seal replacement under 5.2 and an alignment check under 5.4.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The pump ran dry for approximately 10 minutes. The applicable requirement is 'never run dry,' with Plan 11 seal flush supplied from pump discharge; no permissible dry-running duration is documented. The event therefore violated the operating requirement and is relevant to possible seal damage.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal damage is the leading suspected cause of the shaft-area leakage: worn or cracked seal faces and seal dry-running are documented causes. This serial is also within SB-2026-014's population experiencing early HF3-450 seal failure caused by a revised sleeve tolerance; the installed seal type remains to be confirmed.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear is a documented cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature. The above-alarm drive-end temperature also triggers the manual's requirement to replace both bearings as a pair when either shows high temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment is a documented common cause of shaft-seal leakage, high vibration and high bearing temperature, so it could contribute to all three reported symptoms.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage, or cavitation, remains a possible cause of the high vibration; the troubleshooting procedure requires impeller inspection and an NPSH check.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing is a documented possible cause of the high bearing temperature, although it does not by itself explain the seal leakage; grease quantity must be checked.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop P-104 immediately and keep it out of service because the reported vibration is in Zone D. Isolate and drain the pump before starting mechanical-seal work.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Troubleshoot before and during strip-down: confirm the leakage source, check grease quantity and shaft alignment, inspect the bearings and impeller, and check NPSH/cavitation evidence. Record findings to distinguish the remaining probable causes.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Provide lifting equipment for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly. Remove the back pull-out assembly, then remove the impeller nut and impeller following procedure 5.2.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Withdraw the existing seal and shaft sleeve and inspect the sleeve for scoring. Do not fit HF3-450. Install one pre-set HF3-450B cartridge seal, which requires no seal-setting sleeve measurement, together with a new HF3-120 casing gasket. Replace sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Replace drive-end bearing HF3-512 and non-drive-end bearing HF3-510 as a pair because high bearing temperature has occurred; do not replace only the drive-end bearing.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble using the applicable torques. For Table 5 fasteners with lightly oiled threads: M16 casing bolts 210 Nm, M24 impeller nut 160 Nm and M12 bearing-housing bolts 85 Nm. Tighten the HF3-450B seal gland nuts to 30 Nm under SB-2026-014, not the manual's 25 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After work that moves the motor or bearing housing, perform laser shaft alignment. Acceptance tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before restart, confirm the Plan 11 seal-flush arrangement from pump discharge and resolve the tank-changeover condition that allowed dry running. Do not operate the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "On return to service, apply the documented condition limits: measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings, classify the highest reading using Figure 3, stop again for Zone D, and compare housing-surface temperature with the 70°C normal, 80°C alarm and 90°C trip limits. Continue vibration monitoring every week.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C01",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal; mandatory replacement for HF3-450 on this serial-range pump. One seal is required.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; fit new during seal replacement and whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3; replace as part of the bearing pair.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3; replace together with the drive-end bearing.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve; have one available as a conditional part and replace it if inspection shows scoring deeper than 0.1 mm.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Immediate stop is mandatory for the reported Zone D vibration; do not continue restricted operation or merely defer maintenance.",
      "citations": [
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before removing the back pull-out assembly or disturbing the seal.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use lifting equipment for the back pull-out assembly; its documented mass is 68 kg.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Maintain the documented Plan 11 seal-flush arrangement and never run the pump dry, including during tank changeover and return to service.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal replacement: standard labour allowance 4.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement as a pair: standard labour allowance 6.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: standard labour allowance 1.5 hours with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "The manual parts list specifies component seal HF3-450, but SB-2026-014 prohibits fitting that seal on HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above and requires HF3-450B. P-104 is serial HF3-22871, so it is within the bulletin's range; the serial-specific bulletin issued 14 March 2026 governs. Use HF3-450B, not HF3-450.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts, whereas SB-2026-014 gives 30 Nm for HF3-450B. Because P-104 is above serial HF3-22000 and must receive HF3-450B, use 30 Nm. The bulletin explicitly leaves the manual and Table 5 in use only for pumps below that serial threshold; the other applicable Table 5 torques remain unchanged.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Was the reported 7.6 mm/s vibration value measured as RMS velocity as Figure 3 requires, and what is the non-drive-end bearing-housing reading? Only the drive-end value is reported; do not restart the stopped pump solely to obtain another reading.",
    "What seal is currently installed, what is the exact leakage source, and what is the measured sleeve-scoring depth? These findings are needed to confirm the failure history and decide whether the conditional HF3-455 sleeve is required.",
    "What are the actual alignment, grease quantity, bearing and impeller condition, and NPSH/cavitation findings? The evidence cannot determine which of these secondary causes are present or whether the impeller requires replacement.",
    "No numerical acceptable shaft-seal leakage rate or detailed post-repair leakage acceptance test is supplied. The one-drop-per-second report therefore cannot be compared with a numerical leak limit.",
    "What specifically caused the loss of liquid during tank changeover, and what site operating control or protection will prevent recurrence? The evidence states that dry running is prohibited but provides no tank-changeover procedure or dry-run protection settings."
  ]
}
